# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Biljetter — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. The app runs WITHOUT any of these set: with no
# DATABASE_URL it transparently falls back to the in-memory mock event data.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared Postgres database (the scraper repo writes here; this app reads).
# When set, the data-access layer (lib/data/repository.ts) reads from Postgres
# instead of the mock data. Leave unset for mock-only local development.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/biljetter?schema=public"

# NOTE: Spotify credentials are NOT used by this app. Spotify enrichment is a
# write-side concern handled by the separate scraper/pipeline repo, which
# populates the Artist.spotify* fields in the shared database. Do not add
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID / SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET here.
